<SddAmplifyStorage keywords="storage, amplify, schema, indexes, access-patterns, migrations, retention, persistence, sdd-amplify-storage" type="directive" ver="2.0">
  <Mission>
    Deepen the storage model of a scope spec under discovery: schema shape, indexes, access
    patterns, data migrations, retention. Loaded lazily by the discovery interview's triage —
    ONLY for scopes with persistence; inherits the session core — not repeated here.

    Input — the scope spec draft + interview context. Output — a `Storage Model` subsection
    inside the Architecture section of the scope spec + follow-up items on the discovery
    interview map. Out of scope: picking the database engine when the spec already locked it
    (that is a pivot), DDL-level detail — the spec records the model, tickets carry the DDL.
  </Mission>

  <BeliefState deps="AX_OPERATOR_LANGUAGE, AX_OPERATOR_SAFEGUARD, AX_NO_PROCESS_NARRATION">
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-amplify-defaults-first"}}

    {{> "axiom/spec/ax-decision-log-required"}}

    {{> "axiom/spec/ax-access-patterns-drive-schema"}}

    {{> "axiom/spec/ax-data-lifecycle-explicit"}}
  </BeliefState>

  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_NO_PERSISTENCE` | Triage misfired: the scope stores nothing durable — report and return control |
    | `H_OPERATOR_REJECTS_DEFAULTS` | Operator declines the whole defaults package and skips deep-dive — leave the spec untouched |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_0_PROPOSE_DEFAULTS">
      <Goal>Assemble the storage defaults package for this product class.</Goal>
      <Action>
        From the spec draft, list the data the scope persists and — FIRST, per
        `AX_ACCESS_PATTERNS_DRIVE_SCHEMA` — the named access patterns (queries, read/write mix,
        cardinality, hot paths). No durable data → `H_NO_PERSISTENCE`. Per
        `AX_AMPLIFY_DEFAULTS_FIRST`, draft one default decision per topic: schema shape serving
        those patterns, index plan (one named query behind every index), migration policy (expand →
        backfill → contract per `AX_DATA_LIFECYCLE_EXPLICIT`), retention per data class — grounded
        in what live products of this class ship; short targeted research when class practice is
        uncertain.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_1_AGREE">
      <Goal>One accept-or-edit gate; deep-dive only on explicit pick.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Present the package as ONE reply per `AX_AMPLIFY_DEFAULTS_FIRST` (AskUserQuestion when
        available, else `QUESTION_FORMAT`); each topic accept / edit / deep-dive. Deep-dive topic
        map: access patterns → schema → indexes → migrations → retention. Untouched topics keep
        their defaults. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_APPLY">
      <Goal>Write the agreed storage model into the spec.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Write a `### Storage Model` subsection into the Architecture section of the scope spec:
        **Access Patterns** (table `| Запрос | Частота | Read/Write | Hot? |`) → **Schema**
        (entity sketch, intent-level) → **Indexes** (`| Индекс | Обслуживает запрос |`) →
        **Migrations** (policy) → **Retention** (`| Данные | Срок | Механика удаления |`).
        Non-default picks and notable accepted defaults → Decision Log per
        `AX_DECISION_LOG_REQUIRED`. Unresolved topics → items on the discovery interview map.
        Return control to the interview.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>

  <ChatOutput>
    {{> "contract/process/question-format"}}

    Service line — dim, internal, never narrated (`AX_NO_PROCESS_NARRATION`):
    `🗄️ AMP_STO · topics=<n> · accepted=<n> · edited=<n> · dive=<n>`.
  </ChatOutput>
</SddAmplifyStorage>
